## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 · .NET 10 · `[TestCategory("Integration")]`  
**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` (8 test methods)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 101)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` means one branch is always dead — you'll never know if the other path has a bug. The test asserts different things depending on runtime type, hiding gaps.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_AsStandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_AsPremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("prem@example.com", "Prem", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("prem@example.com") as PremiumUser;
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One code path is never validated; false confidence in coverage.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Hard-coded 3-second sleep is non-deterministic. Under load, 3 s may not be enough → flaky. On a fast machine, it wastes 3 s for nothing. This remains a smell even in integration tests because polling/waiters exist.

**Integration calibration:** Acknowledged as integration scope (async event) — severity remains High because deterministic alternatives exist.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of sleeping
    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; 3 s wasted per run; race-condition bugs masked.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion
}
```

**Problem:** If `Insert` silently drops rows, this test still passes. The name implies "no exception = success" but that is insufficient verification.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count, "Not all bulk-inserted users were persisted");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — test passes with broken insert logic.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Smell)

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** Four assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the output is e.g. `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>.` — you must open the source to understand context.

**Fix:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should exist after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip through persistence");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip through persistence");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive auto-increment Id");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage of CI failures; developers must read source to understand what broke.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining 4 tests are well-structured:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|--------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert; single concern |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Verifies absence with `Assert.IsNull` |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count (3) is contextually obvious after 3 inserts — no Magic Number smell |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async/await; verifies final state |

The `[TestInitialize]` setup is a **General Fixture** non-issue: both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | 2 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | 5 min | Split into two focused test methods |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | 10 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-and-timeout helper |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | 3 min | Add message strings to multi-assert tests |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests have cataloged smells. The three High-severity issues (Conditional Logic, Sleepy, Assertion-Free) directly threaten correctness and determinism. The good news: fixes are straightforward and the remaining tests demonstrate solid integration-test design.
